  "verbalization": "Chlorambucil is associated with Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells through a series of indirect pathways involving lymphoma subtypes. The drug is indicated for Richter Syndrome and Follicular Lymphoma, both of which are malignancies of mature B-cells. In these contexts, Chlorambucil is used in combination with other agents, such as Bendamustine or Copanlisib, which are themselves indicated for Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells. This suggests a potential mechanism where Chlorambucil may exert a role in the progression or treatment of these lymphomas, possibly through anti-proliferative or immunomodulatory effects. The evidence is supported by the shared indication for Neoplasm Of Mature B-cells across different therapeutic contexts, indicating a possible overlap in pathophysiological mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential relevance to mature B-cell neoplasms, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated."
